00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:05.390
Couverture chocolate.

00:23:07.270 --> 00:23:11.370
Couverture chocolate is a chocolate that isn't eaten directly;

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:17.200
it is required be processed and heated before being used to make sweets.

00:23:17.520 --> 00:23:20.720
It's a chocolate that pâtissiers embrace.

00:23:21.760 --> 00:23:30.600
Couverture means "to cover up" in French, so it's often used as coating in cakes, cookies and candies.

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:36.870
Furthermore, it's often used in French desserts as dyes.

00:23:38.900 --> 00:23:43.290
There is a very strict international standard for Couverture chocolate.

00:23:43.290 --> 00:23:50.020
If the amount of cacao doesn't inhere to a definite criterion, then the chocolate cannot be called Couverture chocolate.

00:23:51.340 --> 00:23:56.550
Due to its strict standards, it is able to be distinct from other kinds of chocolate.

00:23:56.550 --> 00:23:59.750
It has a perfect texture and viscousness, right!?

